---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  metadata={{
    title: 'About | Patrick O’Dell',
    description: 'Learn more about fantasy and urban fantasy author Patrick O’Dell, creator of The Godfire Saga.',
  }}
>
  <!-- =========================
       ABOUT HERO
  ========================== -->

  <section class="about-hero">
    <div class="container about-hero-grid">
      <!-- AUTHOR IMAGE -->
      <div class="hero-image-wrap">
        <img src="/patrick-odell-author.jpg" alt="Patrick O’Dell Author Portrait" class="hero-image" />
      </div>

      <!-- HERO TEXT -->
      <div class="hero-content">
        <span class="kicker">About the Author</span>

        <h1>Patrick O’Dell</h1>

        <p class="hero-intro">
          Patrick O'Dell is a Baton Rouge author, grant writer, and graduate of the University of Nebraska's MFA in
          Creative Writing program. He began writing at sixteen after an English teacher encouraged him to explore
          storytelling, and he has since created the Godfire Saga, an urban fantasy series following Elias Fetch through
          a world of gods, monsters, and the people caught between them. When he isn't writing, Patrick can usually be
          found reading, gaming, or spending time with his family.
        </p>

        <div class="hero-links">
          <a href="/books" class="btn primary"> Explore the Books </a>

          <a href="/contact" class="btn secondary"> Contact </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- =========================
       MAIN BIOGRAPHY
  ========================== -->

  <section class="about-section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span class="kicker">Biography</span>
        <h2>The Long Story</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="prose-block">
        <p>
          Hi, I'm Patrick O'Dell, a writer from Baton Rouge, Louisiana. I've always loved stories, but I wouldn't be
          where I am today without the people who encouraged me to keep writing.
        </p>

        <p>
          My path wasn't a straight line. I earned my bachelor's degree in Biology (a degree I genuinely value, but
          ultimately, I realized that writing was where I was meant to be). Years later, with Meg's unwavering support
          and the foundation laid by mentors like Dr. Rufleth, Kevin Clouther, and Charlene Donaghy, and many, many
          others, I earned my MFA in Creative Writing from the University of Nebraska Omaha in 2023. My experience at
          UNO was incredible, and I would not be the writer I am today without the influence of the people in that
          program. Today, I'm a grant writer for a nonprofit in Baton Rouge while continuing to create stories that
          explore whatever weird shit my mind manages to scrape together.
        </p>

        <p>Now, to move on to the stuff that is how I am instead of who I am.]</p>

        <p>
          Let me first begin by saying that I have an endless and, at times, invasive curiosity about knowledge and
          learning in general. Things, places, people... if I don't know something, chances are I'm going to want to.
          Smartphones have made that both easier and much, much worse. One innocent question has a habit of turning into
          a three-hour rabbit hole, though life usually finds a way of pulling me back to whatever I was supposed to be
          doing in the first place.
        </p>

        <p>
          That curiosity is what eventually led me to writing. I love understanding how stories work just as much as I
          love telling them. Character voice, worldbuilding, structure, pacing, prose... I'm completely enamored by all
          of it. Give me a beautifully crafted sentence, a perfectly timed twist, or a character who feels undeniably
          real, and I'll probably spend the next hour analyzing how the author pulled it off.
        </p>

        <p>
          Science fiction and fantasy are where I feel most at home because they remove the boundaries of reality
          without removing what makes us human. They let me dive into strange places while asking impossible questions
          and exploring people in situations that could never exist anywhere else. At the end of the day, though, every
          story comes back to the same thing: people.
        </p>

        <p>
          More than anything, I write because it's fun. Stories have an incredible way of making us laugh, wonder, hurt,
          and, if we are lucky, feel a little less alone. If one of mine leaves you curious about life, sparks something
          creative inside you, entertains you, makes you smile, or helps you feel seen in a world that often tries to
          stifle that sense of wonder, then I have done what I set out to do.
        </p>

        <p>
          At the end of the day, my writing is not something I want to keep to myself. Stories are meant to be shared.
          Every world I build, and every journey I create, is an invitation for us to experience something together. I
          hope you have as much fun reading these stories as I have had writing them, and I hope you'll come along for
          whatever adventure comes next.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- =========================
       WRITING FOCUS
  ========================== -->

  <section class="about-section alt">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span class="kicker">Writing</span>
        <h2>Focus & Themes</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="prose-block">
        <p>
          I write science fiction and fantasy because they let me ask very human questions in extraordinary places. I
          love building expansive worlds, weird magic systems, and histories that feel lived in, but those things have
          always been in service of the people who inhabit them. My stories are ultimately about growth, identity, and
          the choices that define us. I'm fascinated by characters who are trying to become better than they were
          yesterday, even when they fail, because that's what being human looks like. Whether they're saving worlds or
          simply trying to find their place within one, I'm interested in the messy, imperfect journey of becoming
          whatever you are meant to be and the path that takes.
        </p>

        <p>
          I tend to gravitate toward writing character-driven stories with equal parts adventure, humor, and heart. My
          protagonists are often irreverent, stubborn, and far more complicated than they'd like anyone to believe.
          They're the sort of people who joke when they're uncomfortable, make questionable decisions with good
          intentions, and spend as much time wrestling with themselves as they do whatever external threat is trying to
          kill them. I enjoy villains whose motivations make you uncomfortable because they make sense and worlds that
          invite you to look in the forests and under rocks. More than anything, I want readers to finish one of my
          books feeling like they've spent time with people they'll remember long after the plot has faded.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- =========================
       CURRENT PROJECTS
  ========================== -->

  <section class="about-section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span class="kicker">Current Projects</span>
        <h2>What I'm Working On</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="project-list">
        <!-- PROJECT -->
        <article class="project-item">
          <h3>Part IV of The Godfire Saga: Sins of the Father</h3>

          <p>
            There are so many things that happen between Gods and Monsters and Sins of the Father, and I wouldn't want
            to spoil anything for anyone interested in reading them, but I will say that I am having a blast watching
            Elias and the others meet new creatures, explore new places, and struggle in new and, unfortunately for
            them, interesting ways.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- =========================
       NEWSLETTER CTA
  ========================== -->

  <section class="about-section newsletter-section">
    <div class="container narrow center">
      <span class="kicker">Newsletter</span>

      <h2>Stay Connected</h2>

      <p class="newsletter-text">
        Stories begin long before they're published. Join my newsletter for updates on upcoming books, behind-the-scenes
        looks at my writing process, exclusive content, and the occasional announcement when a new adventure is ready to
        leave the page.
      </p>

      <!-- REPLACE WITH YOUR NEWSLETTER EMBED -->
      <form class="newsletter-form">
        <input type="email" placeholder="Email address" />

        <button type="submit" class="btn primary"> Subscribe </button>
      </form>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* =========================
   GLOBAL
========================= */

  .container {
    max-width: 1120px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 24px;
  }

  .narrow {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .center {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .about-section {
    padding: 84px 20px;
  }

  .about-section.alt {
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.015), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.01));
  }

  .section-heading {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* =========================
   HERO
========================= */

  .about-hero {
    padding: 70px 20px 90px;
  }

  .about-hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 320px 1fr;
    gap: 60px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .hero-image {
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: 12px;

    box-shadow: 0 28px 80px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.38);
  }

  .hero-content {
    max-width: 620px;
  }

  .hero-intro {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.9;
  }

  .hero-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-top: 28px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  /* =========================
   TYPOGRAPHY
========================= */

  .kicker {
    display: block;

    margin-bottom: 10px;

    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;

    color: rgba(188, 170, 146, 0.58);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    line-height: 1.08;

    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    line-height: 1.15;

    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  h3 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  p {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.9;

    color: rgba(230, 220, 205, 0.8);
  }

  /* =========================
   PROSE
========================= */

  .prose-block {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 22px;
  }

  /* =========================
   PROJECTS
========================= */

  .project-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 36px;
  }

  .project-item {
    padding-bottom: 30px;

    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(210, 198, 178, 0.12);
  }

  .project-item:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  /* =========================
   FACTS
========================= */

  .facts-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 20px;
  }

  .fact-card {
    padding: 22px;

    border: 1px solid rgba(210, 198, 178, 0.12);

    border-radius: 8px;

    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.015);
  }

  .fact-label {
    display: block;

    margin-bottom: 10px;

    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;

    color: rgba(188, 170, 146, 0.58);
  }

  /* =========================
   NEWSLETTER
========================= */

  .newsletter-section {
    padding-bottom: 110px;
  }

  .newsletter-text {
    max-width: 560px;
    margin: 0 auto 28px;
  }

  .newsletter-form {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .newsletter-form input {
    width: 320px;

    padding: 14px 16px;

    border-radius: 6px;

    border: 1px solid rgba(210, 198, 178, 0.18);

    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);

    color: rgba(240, 232, 220, 0.9);
  }

  /* =========================
   BUTTONS
========================= */

  .btn {
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  /* =========================
   RESPONSIVE
========================= */

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .about-hero-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .hero-content {
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .hero-links {
      justify-content: center;
    }

    .hero-image-wrap {
      max-width: 320px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .facts-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: 2rem;
    }

    h2 {
      font-size: 1.55rem;
    }

    .about-section {
      padding: 72px 20px;
    }
  }
</style>
